==English==
{{wikipedia|Endless}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|endeles}}, from {{inh|en|ang|endelēas||endless}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*andijalausaz||endless}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|end|less}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɛndlɪs/|/ˈɛndləs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-endless.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|end|less}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Having no [[end]].
#: {{ux|en|'''endless''' time; '''endless''' praise}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1942|month=May-June|title=Cable Operation at Liverpool and London|journal=Railway Magazine|page=174|text=Trains from Lime Street to Edge Hill were hauled by an '''endless''' hempen rope worked by a stationary engine on the platform at the latter station.}}
# Extending [[indefinite]]ly.
#: {{ux|en|an '''endless''' line}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Without profitable end; fruitless; unsatisfying.
#* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|Love's Pilgrimage|2|3|passage=All loves are '''endless'''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|having no end}} {{l|en|unending}}; see also [[Thesaurus:endless]]
* {{sense|extending indefinitely}} {{l|en|eternal}}, {{l|en|infinite}}, {{l|en|unlimited}}; see also [[Thesaurus:infinite]] or [[Thesaurus:eternal]]

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|finite}}
* {{l|en|limited}}

